1
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,425
[horn honks]

2
00:00:28,366 --> 00:00:33,666
[Jerry] This is a 1964 Morgan Plus 4,
in brilliant blue with a black interior.

3
00:00:34,166 --> 00:00:36,533
It has a four-speed manual gear box...

4
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,633
[engine revs]

5
00:00:37,966 --> 00:00:41,966
...and dual carbs
feeding a 105-horsepower motor.

6
00:00:43,266 --> 00:00:45,100
Morgans are unbelievable cars.

7
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:47,500
They're very British. 
Brits like tradition.

8
00:00:47,566 --> 00:00:51,199
This basic design has been
in production since 1936.

9
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:55,233
The frame is actually made of ash wood,
which makes no sense.

10
00:00:55,366 --> 00:00:56,800
Wood is not for cars.

11
00:00:56,866 --> 00:00:58,833
It's for ventriloquist dummy heads.

12
00:01:00,199 --> 00:01:02,900
These cars are so cool to me
because they just don't care

13
00:01:02,966 --> 00:01:04,733
what the other companies are doing.

14
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,370
A lot like my very special guest today,
Mr. Stephen Colbert...

15
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:13,100
former host of The Colbert Report,

16
00:01:13,166 --> 00:01:16,200
and has recently been picked by CBS
to replace David Letterman

17
00:01:16,266 --> 00:01:18,333
and be their late-night talk show star.

18
00:01:18,533 --> 00:01:21,433
You never told me it was fun!

19
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:24,766
[Jerry] Stephen also looks like
a very conventional, functional person

20
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:27,233
but inside his head, he's a madman.

21
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,266
-Oh, my God.
-Can you dig it?

22
00:01:29,399 --> 00:01:30,766
[phone ringing]

23
00:01:31,133 --> 00:01:32,600
-[Stephen] Hello?
-[Jerry] Stephen?

24
00:01:32,692 --> 00:01:34,794
-[Stephen] Jerry?
-[Jerry] Are your children at home?

25
00:01:34,899 --> 00:01:36,199
[Stephen] No, they're not.

26
00:01:36,266 --> 00:01:38,933
That's an odd lead to a conversation,
I have to say, though.

27
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,333
[Jerry laughs]

28
00:01:40,399 --> 00:01:43,866
[Jerry] I wanted to have breakfast
with somebody amusing, someone witty.

29
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:45,205
[Stephen] I'm out of practice.

30
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:47,740
I haven't had a television show
for almost five months.

31
00:01:47,807 --> 00:01:49,776
[Jerry] Come and see yourself 
as a sports car.

32
00:01:53,633 --> 00:01:58,100
I'm Jerry Seinfeld, and this is
Comedians In Cars Getting Coffee.

33
00:02:05,258 --> 00:02:06,893
-[dog barking]
-Hey.

34
00:02:08,633 --> 00:02:11,100
Scratch, now lick. There it is.

35
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:14,968
[Stephen] Wow...

36
00:02:15,066 --> 00:02:16,966
-Is this original?
-[Jerry] Yeah.

37
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:18,266
It's wood frame,

38
00:02:18,333 --> 00:02:21,666
so you don't have to worry about rust,
but you do have to worry about termites.

39
00:02:21,833 --> 00:02:23,166
[Stephen] It's gorgeous.

40
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:26,212
I want to ask you for a stick of Beemans
before I strap in here.

41
00:02:26,279 --> 00:02:28,948
-I think my beard even matches this.
-[Jerry laughs]

42
00:02:29,033 --> 00:02:31,566
-Whose car is that, the wife?
-[Stephen] That is my daughter's.

43
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:33,319
-Your daughter?
-Soon to be my son's.

44
00:02:33,386 --> 00:02:35,255
-Sex change?
-That's...

45
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:37,833
We don't know.

46
00:02:37,966 --> 00:02:40,966
Is it just a matter of time
before transgender is an airline?

47
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:44,297
You just get on one sex
and you get off, you're the other one.

48
00:02:49,433 --> 00:02:51,733
[Stephen]
It really has that airplane feel to it.

49
00:02:51,799 --> 00:02:54,966
I feel like we're about to fly across
the English Channel

50
00:02:55,033 --> 00:02:57,000
to save the people stranded in Dover.

51
00:02:57,133 --> 00:03:00,066
Perhaps someday we could rent
a cottage on the Isle of Wight.

52
00:03:00,313 --> 00:03:02,582
-If it's not too dear. Yeah.
-If it's not too dear. Exactly.

53
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:08,454
[Jerry] Turn signals,
you're gonna love this.

54
00:03:08,521 --> 00:03:09,589
[clicking]

55
00:03:10,766 --> 00:03:11,766
Here's my horn.

56
00:03:11,933 --> 00:03:12,766
[horn honking]

57
00:03:14,033 --> 00:03:16,933
Would not help you in any way.

58
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:18,666
"We're British, we don't need help.

59
00:03:18,733 --> 00:03:20,799
-We're just fine as we are."
-Everything...

60
00:03:23,937 --> 00:03:26,005
Take out the little book, too,
I love the book.

61
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:29,366
Does it have, like,
a section on etiquette in here?

62
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,366
"Do not interrupt the driver mid-shift."

63
00:03:31,433 --> 00:03:33,500
